---
title: "Style guard"
description: "Restores style utilities that legacy scripts overwrite."
section: Primitives
sectionOrder: 5
order: 0
primitive: style-guard
---

## Example

Load the script once. When the page is ready it starts watching, and from then on it puts back an element's utilities whenever another script replaces its whole `style` attribute.

```html
<script type="module" src="/zazz/primitives/style-guard/style-guard.js"></script>

<div id="banner" style="--p: 4; --bg: var(--color-muted)">Promo</div>
<button type="button" id="legacy">Run the legacy script</button>
<script>
  // a legacy script rewrites the attribute; the guard restores --p and --bg
  document.getElementById("legacy").addEventListener("click", () => {
    document.getElementById("banner").style.cssText = "display: block";
  });
</script>
```

A rewrite that runs before the guard starts (an inline script during page load) wins, because there is nothing to restore yet.

`data-ui-guard="off"` on an element opts it out.

